      "message": "torcontrol: escape backslashes in -torpassword\n\nWith HASHEDPASSWORD authentication the password is sent as a quoted\nstring: AUTHENTICATE \"<password>\". Quotes in the password are escaped,\nbut backslashes aren't. Tor reads a backslash in a quoted string as an\nescape for the next character, so a password like pa\\ss reaches Tor as\n\"pass\" and authentication fails, and a password ending in a backslash\nescapes the closing quote.\n\nEscape backslashes before quotes.",
